    "text": "<p>A hydrocarbon X with formula&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>8</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;uses two moles of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;on catalystic hydrogenation of its one mole. On ozonolysis,&nbsp; X yields two moles of methane dicarbaldehyde. The hydrocarbon is cyclohexa-1,4-diene.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/12f6ea3d-f3d6-4ab4-9b93-f1273bc8a560-9896324.PNG\" style=\"width: 430px; height: 100px;\" /></p>",
